**Read:** [Non-ferrous Extractive Metallurgy — Ray and Pugazhenthy, NPTEL](../sources/Nonferrous-Extractive-Metallurgy-NPTEL.lingua#r_29G1ZF58Y8EG123MNX3ZRNRE2W), the complete magnesium, halide, titanium, and refining sequence; [Principles of Extractive Metallurgy — Tarun Kumar Kundu, NPTEL](../sources/Principles-of-Extractive-Metallurgy-NPTEL.lingua#r_7VCNEHN5VCQDDQTZ512PSHFZ78), all relevant halide-metallurgy and reduction/refining material; [Metals, alloys, steels, and graduate modeling — Bhadeshia teaching materials](../sources/Metals-Alloys-and-Graduate-Teaching-Bhadeshia.lingua#r_0HZJKN8WC6SEWA0DABM8P4HC3F), the full titanium/alloy and high-temperature material; [Metais Não Ferrosos e suas Ligas — Cassio Barbosa](../sources/Metais-Nao-Ferrosos-e-Suas-Ligas-Barbosa.lingua#r_0FJ1378X0JMVHYVBFAXGK2399D), whole titanium and magnesium chapters, when available.

Titanium and magnesium illustrate routes in which feed-compound preparation, halide or other intermediate chemistry, reduction/electrolysis, product separation, and containment/atmosphere are consequential. The route is selected from phase/equilibrium, kinetics, transport, impurities, and the desired product, not from an aqueous standard-potential ranking alone.

Track interstitial and other unwanted elements through feed, reagents, equipment surfaces, atmosphere, residues, and later processing. A chemically reduced product may need further consolidation, melting/refining, and qualified handling before it is useful alloy feed. Processing can introduce or redistribute contamination while changing microstructure.

Compare whole routes with their reagent/energy cycles, recyclable intermediates, equipment materials, phase/product evidence, and professional operational context. A high laboratory chemical yield does not alone establish product integrity, stable production, or a transferable scale.

**Work:** reconstruct a complete titanium or magnesium route and a documented alternative using the full primary technical method. Independently close target and a consequential impurity/reagent account and check the underlying equilibrium/energy basis. Connect measured product chemistry/structure with the process history and receiving fabrication requirement. Explain where further refining, consolidation, atmosphere, or analytical knowledge is needed and what independent evidence could change the comparison.

**Continue:** [Follow specialty metals through chemical similarity, impurity control, and useful product form](Refractory-minor-and-rare-earth-metals-as-separation-problems.lingua#r_64WFPWCN7JW7KG6Y4AN5EJ33CT).

